    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0240" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg120"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Coolidge to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-02-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1813.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the French
                    minister has just notified me that, realizing the interest felt by the American
                    Government in the speedy settlement of the Whangpu conservancy question, as
                    evinced by the instruction of November 19 to the United States diplomatic
                        representatives,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d141-f1"/> he had to inform me that
                    his government had telegraphed its willingness to accept the so-called counter
                    project of the ministers, a copy of which was forwarded to the Department for
                    its approval in my No. 1792 of January 14.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Gardner
                    Coolidge.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
